# Vercel only needs frontend/ (Root Directory is set to "frontend" in
# the project settings) - everything below is backend-only or huge
# binary weights that were force-tracked into git for the separate HF
# Spaces deploy, and would otherwise blow past Vercel's 100MB/file and
# reasonable upload-size limits.
#
# Note: in practice, `vercel --prod` run from the repo root still
# uploaded several GB (models/ + .git's LFS history) despite this file
# - .vercelignore didn't reliably exclude them for a CLI deploy in this
# setup. The approach that actually worked: copy frontend/'s source
# (+ .vercel/project.json) into a clean directory with none of this
# repo's history/weights nearby, and deploy from there instead.
/models/
.git/
.venv/
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/
*.pth
*.joblib
*.caffemodel
/api/
/core/
/core_models/
/db/
/alembic/
/training/
/general_ai/
/inference/
/pipeline/
/evaluation/
/utils/
/docs/
/configs/
/tests/
